n; monitor LFTs. Liposomal Amphotericin B should be reserved for azole failures."}]}, {"id": "body-07713", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Aspiration Syndromes", "runs": [{"text": "Aspiration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Syndromes"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1593"}}, {"id": "body-07714", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Aspiration syndromes are pulmonary conditions caused by inhalation of gastric contents, oropharyngeal secretions, or foreign material into the lower respiratory tract, resulting in chemical lung injury, infection, or airway obstruction.", "runs": [{"text": "Aspiration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndromes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pulmonary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conditions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inhalation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gastric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contents,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oropharyngeal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secretions,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "foreign material into the lower respiratory tract, resulting in chemical lung injury, infection, or airway obstruction."}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Respiratory disease conditions", "start": "body-07700", "end": "body-07714"}}